			"notes": "- Separate singleplayer teleport data per world while preserving legacy data.\n- Add atomic saves, backups, and protection against overwriting unreadable data.\n- Improve Elevator compatibility performance.\n- Recheck permissions and dimensions before teleporting.\n- Fix particle cleanup and clear runtime state on shutdown.\n\nLegacy singleplayer data requires manual import into the correct world (NOT ON SERVERS):\nWorlds no longer share teleport data. Before importing legacy singleplayer data, close the world and copy `config/enderlink/teleports.json` to `saves/<correct-world>/enderlink/teleports.json`.\nBack up any existing destination file first; do not overwrite a world that already has its own pads.\nThe legacy file has no world identifier, so EnderLink never automatically assigns it to a world or deletes it. Keep the original until you have verified the imported pads."
		},
